WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:02.760
Welcome to our year-end review, part two.

00:00:02.760 --> 00:00:06.040
If you’re tuning in for the first time,
this is a special episode during which we

00:00:06.040 --> 00:00:09.440
give you one headline from every country in
the world from the past year.

00:00:09.440 --> 00:00:13.460
The caveat is, hopefully, it’s a headline
you hadn’t heard, and has little to do with

00:00:13.460 --> 00:00:14.460
the C-word.

00:00:14.460 --> 00:00:18.890
We did this last year, and we organized countries
by population size, counting down from largest

00:00:18.890 --> 00:00:19.890
to smallest.

00:00:19.890 --> 00:00:23.519
This year, we are doing a count-up organized
by the Human Development Index, which is a

00:00:23.519 --> 00:00:28.170
number between 0 and 1 determined by the United
Nations based on a series of metrics including

00:00:28.170 --> 00:00:30.170
education, longevity, and earnings.

00:00:30.170 --> 00:00:33.210
We are halfway through the list, and we’ll
end with the country that has the highest

00:00:33.210 --> 00:00:34.520
HDI in the world.

00:00:34.520 --> 00:00:38.400
If you haven’t watched part one, we suggest
you do that too, where we explain the HDI

00:00:38.400 --> 00:00:39.600
breakdown in detail.

00:00:39.600 --> 00:00:43.340
If you’re joining for part two, thanks,
because it means you liked part one.

00:00:43.340 --> 00:00:45.809
Without delay, here’s two.

00:00:45.809 --> 00:00:49.430
Distancing themselves is something that a
Dutch organization is trying to do with Astrid

00:00:49.430 --> 00:00:53.870
Roemer, a poet from the former Dutch colony
of Suriname, after it awarded her with a prestigious

00:00:53.870 --> 00:00:55.710
literary prize earlier this year.

00:00:55.710 --> 00:00:59.739
Recently, she made controversial statements
supporting murderous former president of Suriname

00:00:59.739 --> 00:01:04.220
Desi Bouterse, and the Dutch organizers of
the award chose to forego the ceremony honoring

00:01:04.220 --> 00:01:07.240
her, and simply gave her the cash prize with
little fanfare.

00:01:07.240 --> 00:01:10.760
Roemer, like any real poet, is sticking to
her words.

00:01:10.760 --> 00:01:14.410
Back underground we go, this time to Petite
Mustique, which is part of Saint Vincent and

00:01:14.410 --> 00:01:18.710
the Grenadines, where a human skull was unearthed
on this remote, rugged island in 2003.

00:01:18.710 --> 00:01:23.610
And, this year, researchers at the University
of Oregon may have uncovered why it was there:

00:01:23.610 --> 00:01:27.790
Skeletal abnormalities show the female likely
had leprosy, and this isolated part of the

00:01:27.790 --> 00:01:31.610
Caribbean was probably used to keep people
with the disease away from the public—something

00:01:31.610 --> 00:01:34.770
that many have speculated but this finding
actually supports.

00:01:34.770 --> 00:01:39.799
The skull dates back 200 years and is possibly
the earliest case of leprosy recorded in the

00:01:39.799 --> 00:01:40.799
Americas.

00:01:40.799 --> 00:01:44.200
There is also some speculation that Tunisian
president Kais Saied’s appointment of a

00:01:44.200 --> 00:01:47.750
female prime minister may have been a way
to calm critics who say he’s overreaching

00:01:47.750 --> 00:01:51.090
his power in the Arab Spring’s only remaining
democracy.

00:01:51.090 --> 00:01:55.530
Before Najla Bouden Ramadhane’s appointment,
Saied had already suspended parliament, seized

00:01:55.530 --> 00:01:58.810
power, and fired the previous prime minister,
and because Ramadhane doesn’t have a lot

00:01:58.810 --> 00:02:01.600
of political experience, her trajectory could
be challenging.

00:02:01.600 --> 00:02:05.960
But, she is already making history as the
first female prime minister in the Arab world.

00:02:05.960 --> 00:02:10.229
The Maldives have the unenvious position of
exemplifying climate change’s already dire

00:02:10.229 --> 00:02:14.290
effects on low-lying nations, where 30% of
the country’s annual government budget is

00:02:14.290 --> 00:02:16.750
being spent on adapting to climate change.

00:02:16.750 --> 00:02:20.590
Developed nations have agreed to spend $100
billion to help vulnerable countries adapt,

00:02:20.590 --> 00:02:24.890
but Maldives speaker of parliament wants more;
he’s asking that rich nations also pay reparations

00:02:24.890 --> 00:02:29.209
to help the others deal with the consequences
they’re already suffering—and likely didn’t

00:02:29.209 --> 00:02:30.209
cause.

00:02:30.209 --> 00:02:33.590
Islands in the Caribbean continue to bet big
on tourism, especially countries like Dominica

00:02:33.590 --> 00:02:37.610
which offers Citizenship-by-Investment through
properties like the six-star resort of Secret

00:02:37.610 --> 00:02:38.610
Bay.

00:02:38.610 --> 00:02:42.069
For the fifth year in a row, Dominica was
named the Best Country for Second Citizenship

00:02:42.069 --> 00:02:44.200
by Professional Wealth Management magazine.

00:02:44.200 --> 00:02:47.849
The second-home citizens have primarily come
from Africa, but with a new nonstop flight

00:02:47.849 --> 00:02:51.480
from Miami running, that could potentially
change with Americans starting to look south

00:02:51.480 --> 00:02:53.980
for another home—and passport.

00:02:53.980 --> 00:02:58.129
Added bonus: Dominican residents now get visa-free
access to China.

00:02:58.129 --> 00:03:00.730
When we say coral reef, you probably say,
ugh.

00:03:00.730 --> 00:03:05.379
That’s because a lot of news about the ocean’s
critical habitat for fish species is generally

00:03:05.379 --> 00:03:06.379
bad.

00:03:06.379 --> 00:03:09.349
And that could have been the expectation after
Tropical Cyclone Winston caused more than

00:03:09.349 --> 00:03:14.100
$1.4 billion in damage to Fiji in 2016 and
pummeled the island’s reefs.

00:03:14.100 --> 00:03:17.950
But, they’ve bounced back in a big way as
young coral colonies have taken off, much

00:03:17.950 --> 00:03:21.739
to the delight of researchers, residents,
and likely the colorful fish that have found

00:03:21.739 --> 00:03:22.930
a new home.

00:03:22.930 --> 00:03:26.920
Also in repair are more than a handful of
the 130 precious, historical artifacts that

00:03:26.920 --> 00:03:30.010
were destroyed in the harbor blast in Lebanon
that killed 200 people.

00:03:30.010 --> 00:03:33.770
While the objects pale in comparison to human
lives, their historical significance remains

00:03:33.770 --> 00:03:38.769
important and that’s why the British Museum
granted $29,500 in restoration funds to help

00:03:38.769 --> 00:03:43.349
repair some of the more critical glass vessels
which are nearly 2,000 years old.

00:03:43.349 --> 00:03:47.840
Over on the northwest tip of Africa, an ongoing
conflict between Algeria and Morocco might

00:03:47.840 --> 00:03:49.430
leave Spain in the cold.

00:03:49.430 --> 00:03:53.610
Spain gets about half of its gas from Algeria,
which pumps it through a pipeline in Morocco.

00:03:53.610 --> 00:03:57.629
Morocco depends on Algeria for about 10% of
its gas, and Algeria suspended this pipeline

00:03:57.629 --> 00:04:01.370
to both countries to upset Morocco in an ongoing
territorial dispute.

00:04:01.370 --> 00:04:05.260
It turns out, this may affect Spainiards the
most who will still be able to get gas through

00:04:05.260 --> 00:04:08.459
alternate routes but at much higher prices.

00:04:08.459 --> 00:04:10.290
Moldova is running out of gas too.

00:04:10.290 --> 00:04:14.689
At the end of its contract with Gazprom, Moldova
declared a state of emergency when the Russian

00:04:14.689 --> 00:04:18.250
energy company raised its gas prices and slashed
supply.

00:04:18.250 --> 00:04:22.109
Accused of using gas as leverage, allegations
have surfaced that contract renegotiations

00:04:22.109 --> 00:04:26.130
involved discussion of political issues regarding
Moldova’s separatist region of Transnistria

00:04:26.130 --> 00:04:28.120
and its connection to the EU.

00:04:28.120 --> 00:04:32.220
Associated with the EU, but reliant on Russian
resources, Moldova frequently finds itself

00:04:32.220 --> 00:04:36.040
in the unenviable position of sitting between
east and west.

00:04:36.040 --> 00:04:40.520
From unenviable to regrettable, a mafia fugitive
did himself in by appearing on a YouTube cooking

00:04:40.520 --> 00:04:43.210
show in his adopted home of the Dominican
Republic.

00:04:43.210 --> 00:04:47.210
Though he never showed his face while flashing
his Italian culinary chops, Marc Feren Claude

00:04:47.210 --> 00:04:49.460
Biart’s tattoos gave him away to the police.

00:04:49.460 --> 00:04:52.940
A member of Italy’s largest mafia who fled
Europe when accused of trafficking cocaine

00:04:52.940 --> 00:04:58.020
into the Netherlands, Biart led a quiet, unassuming,
and, in hindsight, too comfortable life in

00:04:58.020 --> 00:04:59.400
the city of Boca Chica.

00:04:59.400 --> 00:05:04.220
An apocalyptic scene unfolded just off the
coast of Azerbaijan as a column of fire blasted

00:05:04.220 --> 00:05:05.420
out of the Caspian Sea.

00:05:05.420 --> 00:05:09.490
While the Caspian is dotted by various offshore
oil rigs, the assumed culprit for the flare

00:05:09.490 --> 00:05:13.580
up wasn’t a leaky Soviet-era pipeline, but
one of the region’s infamous mud volcanoes

00:05:13.580 --> 00:05:14.890
sparking the blast.

00:05:14.890 --> 00:05:18.720
Dubbed the “Land of Fire,” Azerbaijan
is home to major oil reserves and hundreds

00:05:18.720 --> 00:05:21.620
of these mud volcanoes—many of which are
active today.

00:05:21.620 --> 00:05:25.660
What happens underground is also of interest
in St. Lucia, where the Caribbean nation is

00:05:25.660 --> 00:05:28.740
taking the first steps towards harnessing
geothermal energy.

00:05:28.740 --> 00:05:33.080
Currently, St. Lucia relies primarily on diesel
generators for power, so any alternative that

00:05:33.080 --> 00:05:37.039
would alleviate high energy costs is welcomed,
especially one as green as geothermal.

00:05:37.039 --> 00:05:41.300
The next step is figuring out viability—a
project that will be greatly aided by a $22

00:05:41.300 --> 00:05:45.300
million grant made by the World Bank to explore
the potential of the energy source.

00:05:45.300 --> 00:05:49.919
In Ecuador’s most famous islands, Darwin’s
Arch died of natural causes.

00:05:49.919 --> 00:05:54.229
Just a kilometer, or 0.6 miles, off the coast
of Darwin Island in the Galapagos, the arch

00:05:54.229 --> 00:05:57.600
was a popular destination for divers and photographers.

00:05:57.600 --> 00:06:01.430
Ecuadorian officials said that the bridge
was brought down by natural erosion.

00:06:01.430 --> 00:06:04.910
Year by year, though, erosion is becoming
more of a threat and less natural, as volatile

00:06:04.910 --> 00:06:08.950
weather and warming waters are intensifying
the process that created many of the earth’s

00:06:08.950 --> 00:06:10.800
arches in the first place.

00:06:10.800 --> 00:06:13.520
Another troubling trend came to a head in
China.

00:06:13.520 --> 00:06:17.180
Birthrates in the world’s most populous
country hit an all-time low since the country

00:06:17.180 --> 00:06:20.139
began tabulating the figure in 1978.

00:06:20.139 --> 00:06:23.710
Infamous for its “one child” policy, China
has been easing restrictions on family-size

00:06:23.710 --> 00:06:27.710
since 2015 as dropping birth rates began to
worry state officials.

00:06:27.710 --> 00:06:31.199
This year’s low water mark, though, hints
that the problem may be beyond policy and

00:06:31.199 --> 00:06:34.819
expected demographic shifts as the country
develops, and more so a function of rising

00:06:34.819 --> 00:06:38.680
cost of living and financial insecurity pushing
potential parents to hold off.

00:06:38.680 --> 00:06:42.319
Birds, too, are adapting to changing material
living conditions.

00:06:42.319 --> 00:06:47.000
A study of 77 non-migratory birds undertaken
in Brazil has shown that each species has

00:06:47.000 --> 00:06:50.190
become smaller in stature over the past 40
years.

00:06:50.190 --> 00:06:54.040
This finding in species confined to remote
areas of the Amazon has allowed researchers

00:06:54.040 --> 00:06:58.479
to conclude that the shrinking is in response
to the one major alteration in their environment:

00:06:58.479 --> 00:06:59.479
temperature rise.

00:06:59.479 --> 00:07:02.960
While researches haven’t come to a consensus,
it’s hypothesized that the birds are slimming

00:07:02.960 --> 00:07:06.750
down because they simply aren’t required
to generate the same body heat as in decades

00:07:06.750 --> 00:07:09.130
prior––humans are doing it for them.

00:07:09.130 --> 00:07:14.090
A decision made by Colombia’s congress gave
Viche, often referred to as “African-Colombian

00:07:14.090 --> 00:07:17.639
Moonshine,” its well-deserved moment in
the sun.

00:07:17.639 --> 00:07:21.419
Recognizing the liquor distilled from sugar
cane by generations of African Colombians

00:07:21.419 --> 00:07:25.270
as a piece of the country’s “ancestral
and cultural heritage,” is an honor, and

00:07:25.270 --> 00:07:27.190
for many, an opportunity.

00:07:27.190 --> 00:07:31.250
Increased notoriety, experts believe, will
provide an opportunity for distillers to capitalize

00:07:31.250 --> 00:07:35.610
on the product–giving it the chance to follow
the same trajectory as Mezcal in Mexico and

00:07:35.610 --> 00:07:37.570
to create generational wealth locally.

00:07:37.570 --> 00:07:42.680
While other parts of former Yugoslavia threatened
to fall apart, North Macedonia celebrated

00:07:42.680 --> 00:07:47.940
2021 as the year marked the 30th anniversary
of its peacefully-established independence.

00:07:47.940 --> 00:07:52.410
A military parade through the capital of Skopje
and celebrations across the country marked

00:07:52.410 --> 00:07:53.410
the occasion.

00:07:53.410 --> 00:07:57.620
While independent for decades, integration
into the West has been a winding road as disputes

00:07:57.620 --> 00:08:01.820
with Greece saw the country relinquish its
original name, Macedonia, for its current

00:08:01.820 --> 00:08:03.389
moniker.

00:08:03.389 --> 00:08:07.199
Another milestone was reached this year when
Joe Biden became the first US President to

00:08:07.199 --> 00:08:10.750
acknowledge that the Armenian Genocide was
in fact a genocide.

00:08:10.750 --> 00:08:15.319
In Armenia, and across the Armenian diaspora,
the news was welcomed with a tepid response

00:08:15.319 --> 00:08:19.330
not because of the 106 years of separation
from the event, but because the declaration

00:08:19.330 --> 00:08:21.900
is, of course, merely a declaration.

00:08:21.900 --> 00:08:25.470
Many see the statement as a symbolic gesture
designed to test the relationship with Turkey

00:08:25.470 --> 00:08:29.180
who has yet to qualify the historical atrocity
as a genocide.

00:08:29.180 --> 00:08:33.940
A move that may have large repercussions caught
the eye of free speech advocates world-wide

00:08:33.940 --> 00:08:38.599
when Thailand’s government banned the dissemination
of news that “causes public fear.”

00:08:38.599 --> 00:08:42.370
The government framed the mandate as a move
to limit the dangerous spread of disinformation

00:08:42.370 --> 00:08:44.240
but critics see it differently.

00:08:44.240 --> 00:08:47.950
The ban, which allows the government to block
individual’s internet access, conveniently

00:08:47.950 --> 00:08:53.220
materialized just as criticism with the government’s
slow rollout of vaccines hit fever pitch.

00:08:53.220 --> 00:08:57.810
For Peru’s conservative right, there’s
been no escaping fear-inducing news in 2021,

00:08:57.810 --> 00:09:02.320
as a narrow election saw the swearing in of
socialist president Pedro Castillo.

00:09:02.320 --> 00:09:06.690
The rise of the rural teacher-turned-politician
caught the world off guard and certainly didn’t

00:09:06.690 --> 00:09:09.970
sit well with the country’s established
power brokers who immediately contested the

00:09:09.970 --> 00:09:13.050
result and whose supporters harassed election
officials.

00:09:13.050 --> 00:09:17.300
Only months in, Castillo’s presidency is
barely holding on as his approval rating has

00:09:17.300 --> 00:09:20.770
plummeted and a possible move to impeach hangs
in the balance.

00:09:20.770 --> 00:09:25.320
A world record also hung in the balance this
year as spectators along an Antiguan harbor

00:09:25.320 --> 00:09:29.320
anxiously awaited the appearance of Jasmine
Harrison’s rowboat on the horizon.

00:09:29.320 --> 00:09:32.950
She and her boat eventually pulled into the
waters of Antigua and Barbuda, the nation

00:09:32.950 --> 00:09:36.760
that marks the finish line of the Talisker
Whiskey Atlantic Challenge, and Harrison became

00:09:36.760 --> 00:09:41.560
the youngest woman to row the Atlantic solo—a
70-day-long odyssey that saw her thrown overboard

00:09:41.560 --> 00:09:44.070
twice and her mettle tested constantly.

00:09:44.070 --> 00:09:47.830
Coming to the end of their own odyssey is
the “Scythian Gold.”

00:09:47.830 --> 00:09:51.570
This year, A Dutch court ruled that the trove
of Crimean treasures dating back to the days

00:09:51.570 --> 00:09:54.529
of the Silk Road rightfully belonged to Ukraine.

00:09:54.529 --> 00:09:58.870
On display in 2014 when Russia annexed the
peninsula, the fate of these cultural artifacts

00:09:58.870 --> 00:10:01.800
had been in limbo for years before this ruling.

00:10:01.800 --> 00:10:05.610
Russia has criticized the ruling, while Ukraine
has labeled it another recognition of the

00:10:05.610 --> 00:10:08.720
world’s condemnation over Russia’s seizure
of the peninsula.

00:10:08.720 --> 00:10:11.120
In Saint Kitts and Nevis, the story’s apiculture.

00:10:11.120 --> 00:10:16.180
Now if you aren’t a former geo-bee champion
with an expansive vocabulary, you may not

00:10:16.180 --> 00:10:18.829
recognize the place nor the practice.

00:10:18.829 --> 00:10:23.290
All the same, the Caribbean nation of 50,000
joined an international effort to help launch

00:10:23.290 --> 00:10:25.600
and support local bee-keeping businesses.

00:10:25.600 --> 00:10:29.480
If properly executed, the initiative will
create additional jobs, bring local honey

00:10:29.480 --> 00:10:34.410
and wax products to market, and help protect
biodiversity by keeping pollinators, well,

00:10:34.410 --> 00:10:35.410
buzzing.

00:10:35.410 --> 00:10:40.260
West of where a bulk of bees are set to soon
buzz, Mexican politicians and activists battled.

00:10:40.260 --> 00:10:45.000
After much debate, it was announced that Mexico’s
150-year-old Columbus statue was to be replaced

00:10:45.000 --> 00:10:47.170
by a statue of an indigenous woman.

00:10:47.170 --> 00:10:51.490
A reasonable decision at surface level, and
one that recognizes two oft-overlooked groups

00:10:51.490 --> 00:10:55.480
in Mexico, women and indigenous people, some
see the move as political posturing by Mayor

00:10:55.480 --> 00:10:59.620
Claudie Sheinbaum—one that wins her positive
PR without actually helping the plight of

00:10:59.620 --> 00:11:02.290
indigenous Mexicans or women.

00:11:02.290 --> 00:11:06.290
From statues in metaphorical hot water to
those physically under it, Grenada announced

00:11:06.290 --> 00:11:09.829
the completion of a renovation to its underwater
sculpture park.

00:11:09.829 --> 00:11:13.840
Repairs and cleaning of already existing sculptures
were part of the project, but the most exciting

00:11:13.840 --> 00:11:18.209
bit was the new 82-piece installation celebrating
Grenadian culture.

00:11:18.209 --> 00:11:22.600
Since its creation in 2006, the park has offered
habitat for marine wildlife and served as

00:11:22.600 --> 00:11:26.870
an important tourist draw—the renovation
aims to maintain that positive momentum.

00:11:26.870 --> 00:11:31.360
Though hard to imagine, things are getting
more complicated in a country with two names

00:11:31.360 --> 00:11:32.920
and three presidents.

00:11:32.920 --> 00:11:37.610
Calling it an “existential threat,” one
top American diplomat flew to Bosnia-Herzegovina

00:11:37.610 --> 00:11:41.991
to coax Bosnian Serb leader, Milorad Dodik,
to lighten his separatist rhetoric that, if

00:11:41.991 --> 00:11:45.980
acted upon, would potentially nose-dive the
nation and destabilize the region.

00:11:45.980 --> 00:11:50.589
The epicenter of ethnic violence in the mid-1990s
that took painstaking negotiations to quell,

00:11:50.589 --> 00:11:55.089
a separatist move like the one Dodik threatens
would set the region back decades.

00:11:55.089 --> 00:11:59.530
If nothing else good came of it, the pandemic
offered zoo animals a well-earned rest.

00:11:59.530 --> 00:12:04.510
In Sri Lanka, where zoos closed in March of
2020 and have only briefly opened since, animals

00:12:04.510 --> 00:12:08.399
have taken the newfound peace and quiet to
deepen relationships and spend a lot of time

00:12:08.399 --> 00:12:09.399
in bed.

00:12:09.399 --> 00:12:14.140
The result was a baby boom, as some species—the
black swan and white peacock—mated in Sri

00:12:14.140 --> 00:12:18.260
Lankan zoos for the first time ever, while
others such as lions, have accelerated their

00:12:18.260 --> 00:12:21.779
output in lieu of nosey-onlookers.

00:12:21.779 --> 00:12:25.529
Perhaps the world could’ve used a few more
nosey onlookers in the Sea of Oman this year

00:12:25.529 --> 00:12:29.959
as noted not-friends Iran and the US offered
wildly different accounts as to what really

00:12:29.959 --> 00:12:33.529
happened when Iran seized an oil tanker just
off its coast.

00:12:33.529 --> 00:12:37.100
Iran officials claimed that the US had taken
their tanker before their successful naval

00:12:37.100 --> 00:12:41.400
assault reclaimed the ship, while US officials
say that it was a Vietnamese tanker that Iran

00:12:41.400 --> 00:12:42.690
had seized.

00:12:42.690 --> 00:12:46.620
Regardless of who’s telling the truth, this
most recent rift offers a reminder of just

00:12:46.620 --> 00:12:50.500
how rocky the relations between the two nations
remain.

00:12:50.500 --> 00:12:52.770
Cuban officials wouldn’t be fooled twice
this year.

00:12:52.770 --> 00:12:56.650
After the largest protests in 30 years caught
them off guard this July, the government made

00:12:56.650 --> 00:13:00.000
sure to stamp out the next protest before
it even started.

00:13:00.000 --> 00:13:04.639
As news spread of a potential pro-democracy,
freedom of expression demonstration, the state

00:13:04.639 --> 00:13:08.170
didn’t let noted protesters leave their
homes, arrested congregators, and released

00:13:08.170 --> 00:13:12.760
media claiming that protests were an attempt
of regime change by the hands of the US.

00:13:12.760 --> 00:13:16.959
One European country has proved especially
welcoming to Afghan refugees, and it’s one

00:13:16.959 --> 00:13:18.800
of the continent’s poorest.

00:13:18.800 --> 00:13:22.970
Albania, bolstered by a culture familiar with
and receptive to immigrants, pledged to take

00:13:22.970 --> 00:13:25.579
in as many as 4,000 Afghans.

00:13:25.579 --> 00:13:30.380
The nearly 700 that made it to the coastal
nation were put up in beach-side resorts.

00:13:30.380 --> 00:13:34.589
Albania is likely just a year-long stop for
refugees as they seek to secure visas to countries

00:13:34.589 --> 00:13:37.970
that offer more opportunity, but Albania has
made it clear that they’re more than welcome

00:13:37.970 --> 00:13:40.320
to stay should they want to.

00:13:40.320 --> 00:13:44.490
Michael B. Jordan understands firsthand the
baggage that comes with a name.

00:13:44.490 --> 00:13:48.369
Perhaps that’s why the actor was willing
to change the name of his new rum brand, initially

00:13:48.369 --> 00:13:52.070
called “J’Ouvert” once Trinidad and
Tobagonians took offense to his trademarking

00:13:52.070 --> 00:13:55.339
the term that refers to the opening of their
famed Carnival.

00:13:55.339 --> 00:13:59.279
Labeling the act as cultural appropriation,
thousands from Trinidad and Tobago signed

00:13:59.279 --> 00:14:03.839
an online petition to protect and respect
a word that means so much to their culture

00:14:03.839 --> 00:14:07.240
The Coco de Mer, a palm tree that produces
the world’s largest—and subjectively,

00:14:07.240 --> 00:14:10.889
the most inappropriate—seed in the world,
only exists in Seychelles.

00:14:10.889 --> 00:14:15.920
In fact, the tree only grows on two of the
archipelago’s 115 islands while the rare

00:14:15.920 --> 00:14:20.670
seed, sold mostly to bemused tourists, fetches
up to $260.

00:14:20.670 --> 00:14:24.820
Beloved by islanders, heavily regulated by
the government, and yet still endangered,

00:14:24.820 --> 00:14:29.029
Seychelles is taking a new approach to conserving
the tree by putting seeds in the hands of

00:14:29.029 --> 00:14:30.029
locals.

00:14:30.029 --> 00:14:33.139
Those interested in growing the tree on their
property can apply for the honor and must

00:14:33.139 --> 00:14:37.269
prove they have enough room and the right
soil for the palm to take off.

00:14:37.269 --> 00:14:41.580
Sending mail to the Chagos archipelago became
a bit more difficult this year.

00:14:41.580 --> 00:14:44.970
Recognizing Mauritius' sovereignty over the
chain of islands that’s now one of Britain’s

00:14:44.970 --> 00:14:49.180
last and most controversial colonial holdings,
the UN’s postal union decided it would no

00:14:49.180 --> 00:14:53.150
longer recognize postage stamps issued by
the “British Indian Overseas Territories

00:14:53.150 --> 00:14:54.150
of the UK.”

00:14:54.150 --> 00:14:57.940
This move adds ever so slightly to the pressure
on Britain to leave the chain and represents

00:14:57.940 --> 00:15:02.029
another baby step towards returning home for
Chagossians forcibly relocated to Mauritius

00:15:02.029 --> 00:15:03.709
decades ago.

00:15:03.709 --> 00:15:07.440
Cristiano Ronaldo couldn’t wait to get home
after a controversial call in Serbia cost

00:15:07.440 --> 00:15:10.810
him and his country important World Cup qualifying
points.

00:15:10.810 --> 00:15:15.230
However, throwing his captain’s armband
down in disgust as he exited the pitch unintentionally

00:15:15.230 --> 00:15:20.670
did a world of good for a six-month-old Serbian
boy with spinal muscular atrophy.

00:15:20.670 --> 00:15:24.500
Donated to a charity group who then auctioned
off the armband, Ronaldo’s frustration resulted

00:15:24.500 --> 00:15:30.720
in a $71,000 haul—money which went directly
to the six-month-old’s treatment.

00:15:30.720 --> 00:15:34.449
In Kuwait, things aren’t looking quite as
dire for those nearing the other end of the

00:15:34.449 --> 00:15:38.600
age spectrum as the country’s legislature
reversed a ban on employing expatriates over

00:15:38.600 --> 00:15:40.250
the age of 60.

00:15:40.250 --> 00:15:44.360
Struck down because it had no legal basis,
the ruling serves as just a respite for the

00:15:44.360 --> 00:15:48.070
nation’s expat population who have been
leaving by the thousands as the state continues

00:15:48.070 --> 00:15:52.490
to push for the development of its domestic
workforce through its years-long “Kuwaitization”

00:15:52.490 --> 00:15:53.490
project.

00:15:53.490 --> 00:15:57.370
A more substantial legal ruling was recorded
this year in Malaysia as the country’s highest

00:15:57.370 --> 00:16:01.840
court ruled that the Islamic provision that
banned same sex acts was unconstitutional.

00:16:01.840 --> 00:16:06.610
LGBTQ advocates have called the ruling “historic”
as the country’s experienced an uptick in

00:16:06.610 --> 00:16:09.130
homophobic sentiment in recent years.

00:16:09.130 --> 00:16:13.910
This ruling though, does not legalize same-sex
acts, as a civil law from Britain’s colonial-era

00:16:13.910 --> 00:16:16.830
banning those is still on the books.

00:16:16.830 --> 00:16:20.770
Costa Rica earned some well-deserved national
attention when the country was named one of

00:16:20.770 --> 00:16:25.270
the five winners of the Earthshot Prize—a
global sustainability effort spearheaded by

00:16:25.270 --> 00:16:27.759
Prince William and Kate Middleton.

00:16:27.759 --> 00:16:32.529
Financed largely by taxes on fossil fuels,
Costa Rica has handed more than $500 million

00:16:32.529 --> 00:16:36.740
to landowners over the last 20 years to protect
forests and watersheds.

00:16:36.740 --> 00:16:40.110
The effort has largely reversed deforestation
in the country.

00:16:40.110 --> 00:16:44.459
While the prize money is nice, the international
recognition serves as a proof of concept for

00:16:44.459 --> 00:16:49.029
other nations and a pat on the back for forward-thinking
Costa Rica.

00:16:49.029 --> 00:16:51.950
Forward-thinking was the praise Georgia thought
it might reap when the country broke ground

00:16:51.950 --> 00:16:55.660
on its “hypermodern” parliament building
a decade ago.

00:16:55.660 --> 00:17:00.190
Today though, it sits empty, and its glass
windows meant to signal governmental transparency

00:17:00.190 --> 00:17:01.190
gather dust.

00:17:01.190 --> 00:17:05.079
Done in by its distance from the capital and
the new political regime’s distaste for

00:17:05.079 --> 00:17:09.650
it, the building was abandoned in 2018, then
put up for sale through May of 2021, when

00:17:09.650 --> 00:17:12.949
the government finally gave up on finding
a buyer.

00:17:12.949 --> 00:17:17.669
As Georgia gave up on its governmental greenhouse,
Oman announced their aim to build a massive

00:17:17.669 --> 00:17:19.560
green hydrogen plant.

00:17:19.560 --> 00:17:23.980
Oman’s following the forward-thinking theme
by working to smooth an impending economic

00:17:23.980 --> 00:17:28.250
transition, as 85% of the country’s GDP
is generated from oil and gas—resources

00:17:28.250 --> 00:17:30.290
which the country’s quickly running out
of.

00:17:30.290 --> 00:17:34.630
Powered by wind and solar, it is hoped that
the $30 billion project will be producing

00:17:34.630 --> 00:17:38.280
and exporting renewable energy at full capacity
by 2038.

00:17:38.280 --> 00:17:42.140
In the very same year that Barbados ended
symbolic ties with the Queen of England and

00:17:42.140 --> 00:17:47.260
became a republic, the nation’s most famous
export, Rihanna, became a national hero.

00:17:47.260 --> 00:17:51.601
Well, technically the artist, entrepreneur,
and proud bajan has been a national icon in

00:17:51.601 --> 00:17:55.760
the country for more than a decade, but this
year her legendary status became official

00:17:55.760 --> 00:17:59.500
when the new republic’s prime minister designated
her a national hero.

00:17:59.500 --> 00:18:03.390
Already an ambassador for the Caribbean country,
and recently named the world’s richest female

00:18:03.390 --> 00:18:07.390
musician, it seems that Rihanna’s reign
just won’t let up–and Barbados is all

00:18:07.390 --> 00:18:09.140
the better for it.

00:18:09.140 --> 00:18:14.080
At the other end of the Caribbean, three Cubans
survived 33 days on a barren Bahamian island

00:18:14.080 --> 00:18:16.540
before being rescued by the US Coast Guard.

00:18:16.540 --> 00:18:20.660
After capsizing at sea, likely in an attempt
to flee Cuba, the three washed up on one of

00:18:20.660 --> 00:18:25.720
the least-hospitable Bahamas, surviving on
coconut water, conch shells, and rats.

00:18:25.720 --> 00:18:29.470
After receiving brief medical attention in
Florida, the resourceful survivors were handed

00:18:29.470 --> 00:18:32.430
over to US Immigration and Customs Enforcement.

00:18:32.430 --> 00:18:35.500
This isn’t the first time The Bahamas have
found itself as the meeting point between

00:18:35.500 --> 00:18:40.450
Cuban defectors and the US, as a similar rescue
took place a few islands over not months before

00:18:40.450 --> 00:18:41.450
this one.

00:18:41.450 --> 00:18:45.240
The Bahamas have hardly been the focal point
for dangerous American migrations, though.

00:18:45.240 --> 00:18:49.710
It’s been a record-breaking year for Panama
immigration officials as a whopping 70,000

00:18:49.710 --> 00:18:54.039
migrants from around the world have passed
through the Darien Gap and into the country.

00:18:54.039 --> 00:18:58.590
Such incredible numbers making their way through
the undeveloped, densely forested, and crime-riddled

00:18:58.590 --> 00:19:03.120
route with no formal roadways has pushed Panamanian
and Colombian officials to begin regulating

00:19:03.120 --> 00:19:08.060
the number of entrants into the Darien Gap—potentially
a first step in making the journey safer for

00:19:08.060 --> 00:19:10.260
the desperate migrants.

00:19:10.260 --> 00:19:13.610
International collaboration was the context
that informed an embarrassing development

00:19:13.610 --> 00:19:14.820
in Bulgaria.

00:19:14.820 --> 00:19:19.850
Led by the US Army, the NATO military exercise
called Swift Response brought together 7,000

00:19:19.850 --> 00:19:23.350
paratroopers from 10 member nations for some
joint practice.

00:19:23.350 --> 00:19:27.480
Swift Response, though, quickly became seriously
regrettable when American soldiers accidently

00:19:27.480 --> 00:19:32.400
left the training zone and barged into and
cleared out a Bulgarian sunflower oil factory.

00:19:32.400 --> 00:19:36.520
The factory has since filed a lawsuit, while
the US embassy, for its part, has apologized

00:19:36.520 --> 00:19:38.400
for the mistake.

00:19:38.400 --> 00:19:42.160
Netflix further expanded its reach when it
greenlit the company’s first feature-length

00:19:42.160 --> 00:19:43.830
film shot in Uruguay.

00:19:43.830 --> 00:19:48.200
The company’s VP of Latin American content
has hailed the project as an exciting opportunity

00:19:48.200 --> 00:19:50.270
to highlight the creative talent in the country.

00:19:50.270 --> 00:19:54.570
While it’s unlikely that viewers will recognize
names when the credits roll, the film, titled

00:19:54.570 --> 00:19:58.670
Togo, will fit right in the current cinematic
canon as the crime drama revolves around street-level

00:19:58.670 --> 00:20:01.549
drug trafficking and organized crime.

00:20:01.549 --> 00:20:05.140
Following the appearance of mysterious metallic
monoliths across the American West and in

00:20:05.140 --> 00:20:08.600
Romania, a similar structure appeared in southwest
Turkey.

00:20:08.600 --> 00:20:13.000
But this one came with a message in ancient
Turkish: “look at the sky, and you will

00:20:13.000 --> 00:20:14.000
see the moon.”

00:20:14.000 --> 00:20:17.470
Residents didn’t have to wait long on an
explanation as to the origins of the structure

00:20:17.470 --> 00:20:21.790
and its innocuous truism though, as only days
after its discovery, President Erdoğan used

00:20:21.790 --> 00:20:26.110
the monolith as a background when he announced
the country’s new space program and 10-year

00:20:26.110 --> 00:20:30.010
vision—proving the monolith’s function
as an eye-rolling gimmick.

00:20:30.010 --> 00:20:34.620
Bucking tradition at the Tokyo Olympics, one
sprinter, rather than running for her country,

00:20:34.620 --> 00:20:36.210
ran away from it.

00:20:36.210 --> 00:20:39.450
Accusing her coaches of negligence before
being pulled from her event and pressured

00:20:39.450 --> 00:20:44.039
to return home to Belarus, Krystsina Tsimanouskaya
fled to the Polish embassy where she was granted

00:20:44.039 --> 00:20:45.650
a humanitarian visa.

00:20:45.650 --> 00:20:50.260
The incident exemplifies the mounting pressure
on Belarussian public figures under the country’s

00:20:50.260 --> 00:20:54.289
increasingly authoritarian government as she
joins a growing list of athletes, coaches,

00:20:54.289 --> 00:20:58.520
and high-profile Belarussians that have faced
job loss, arrest, or imprisonment when voicing

00:20:58.520 --> 00:21:01.789
discontent with the government in the past
two years.

00:21:01.789 --> 00:21:05.610
State overreach is also the fear in Russia,
as the Moscow metro has implemented a new

00:21:05.610 --> 00:21:09.250
method of payment at over 240 stations called
Face Pay.

00:21:09.250 --> 00:21:13.630
As the program’s name suggests, Moscow commuters
can now leave their phone and wallet at home

00:21:13.630 --> 00:21:15.740
and simply smile for the camera to board the
train.

00:21:15.740 --> 00:21:19.560
In a country where governmental transparency
is hard to come by and facial recognition

00:21:19.560 --> 00:21:23.880
has been allegedly used to identify protestors,
Face Pay has human rights groups and dubious

00:21:23.880 --> 00:21:27.770
citizens concerned by the project’s potential
ulterior motives.

00:21:27.770 --> 00:21:31.500
In another former Soviet state, government
officials made a statement as to where their

00:21:31.500 --> 00:21:36.410
current allegiances lie when they kicked out
an outspoken US, Russian dual national.

00:21:36.410 --> 00:21:40.570
Receiving a letter notifying he was barred
from entry into Kazakhstan, Gene Bunin, who

00:21:40.570 --> 00:21:44.809
founded a victims database to track the incarceration
of Uyghurs in western China, serves as an

00:21:44.809 --> 00:21:48.950
example as to how closely Kazakhstan has come
to align itself with China, not only turning

00:21:48.950 --> 00:21:53.250
a blind eye to the what the US and UN have
come to define as genocide, but now seemingly

00:21:53.250 --> 00:21:56.120
helping to quiet dissent within its own borders.

00:21:56.120 --> 00:22:00.580
While some bonds are strengthening in Central
Asia, others in the Pacific are beginning

00:22:00.580 --> 00:22:01.720
to crumble.

00:22:01.720 --> 00:22:05.620
The result of a vote on the new secretary
general for the Pacific Islands Forum was

00:22:05.620 --> 00:22:09.610
the last straw for the tiny Micronesian country
of Palau who announced they’d be leaving

00:22:09.610 --> 00:22:10.740
the organization.

00:22:10.740 --> 00:22:14.740
The coalition long had an informal tradition
of rotating its secretary general position

00:22:14.740 --> 00:22:19.650
between Micronesian, Polynesian, and Melanesian
politicians, but the election of a Cook Islands

00:22:19.650 --> 00:22:23.970
politician was a break from convention that
left Micronesian nations like Palau, and other

00:22:23.970 --> 00:22:27.980
small island states that would follow their
lead, feeling slighted and voiceless in the

00:22:27.980 --> 00:22:29.470
organization’s proceedings.

00:22:29.470 --> 00:22:33.640
Trophy hunting of large carnivores is banned
in Romania but that didn’t stop Prince Emanuel

00:22:33.640 --> 00:22:38.380
von und zu Liechtenstein of Austria from shooting
the country’s, and potentially the European

00:22:38.380 --> 00:22:40.270
Union’s, single largest brown bear.

00:22:40.270 --> 00:22:43.880
While the prince had authorization from the
Romanian government to hunt a female nuisance

00:22:43.880 --> 00:22:48.850
bear causing problems for a small farm town,
he managed to bag the massive 17-year-old

00:22:48.850 --> 00:22:53.000
Arthur—whether by accident or intentionally
is under investigation.

00:22:53.000 --> 00:22:57.059
In another mountainous eastern European country,
construction crews put the finishing touches

00:22:57.059 --> 00:23:00.490
on a state-of-the-art highway that cuts through
rugged Montenegro.

00:23:00.490 --> 00:23:04.110
Rather than celebrating though, residents
are beginning to ask questions about the road’s

00:23:04.110 --> 00:23:08.200
$1 billion price tag—the road only connects
a few small communities including the town

00:23:08.200 --> 00:23:10.770
at its terminus, Matesevo, home to a population
of 15.

00:23:10.770 --> 00:23:16.710
An early Belt and Road project built by Chinese
crews, Montenegro’s finances are now seriously

00:23:16.710 --> 00:23:20.570
strained by the road that really doesn’t
serve much of a purpose.

00:23:20.570 --> 00:23:25.530
The people of Brunei are hoping for more sage
decision-making from the new CEO of the nation’s

00:23:25.530 --> 00:23:28.909
largest financial institution, Bank Islam
Brunei Darussalam.

00:23:28.909 --> 00:23:33.940
Hjh Noriani will be the first female CEO of
the bank that manages $10 billion of assets

00:23:33.940 --> 00:23:38.060
and has expanded across Southeast Asia and
into the Middle East in recent years.

00:23:38.060 --> 00:23:42.720
After naming three women to top positions
in 2019, the move follows an empowering trend

00:23:42.720 --> 00:23:45.660
at the bank in the traditionally conservative
country.

00:23:45.660 --> 00:23:51.740
In Argentina, a 30-year-old confirmed an age-old
maxim: if it’s too good to be true, it usually

00:23:51.740 --> 00:23:52.740
is.

00:23:52.740 --> 00:23:56.159
Searching for an explanation for a momentary
Google outage, Nicolas Kuroña found that

00:23:56.159 --> 00:24:01.539
the domain google.com.ar had expired and that
he could buy it for a modest $2.60.

00:24:01.539 --> 00:24:06.390
The Argentine quickly scooped up the domain
that, if everything broke his way, could be

00:24:06.390 --> 00:24:08.210
worth millions.

00:24:08.210 --> 00:24:12.049
The domain didn’t prove a golden ticket
though, but a mistake as Google’s ownership

00:24:12.049 --> 00:24:16.710
hadn’t lapsed, and in the end, Kuroña came
out of the situation a few dollars lighter.

00:24:16.710 --> 00:24:20.799
In a country that’s been in the headlines
for all the wrong reasons the past few years

00:24:20.799 --> 00:24:23.130
has emerged a more positive story.

00:24:23.130 --> 00:24:27.450
Rolls-Royce and Qatar announced a multi-year,
multi-billion-dollar partnership aimed to

00:24:27.450 --> 00:24:29.610
foster green technology companies.

00:24:29.610 --> 00:24:34.020
The partnership will build two campuses, one
in each country; create an estimated 1,000

00:24:34.020 --> 00:24:37.920
jobs; and hopefully provide the resources
and facilities for sustainability-oriented

00:24:37.920 --> 00:24:39.580
startups to take off.

00:24:39.580 --> 00:24:45.180
Prošek and Prosecco are two different types
of wine with two different names.

00:24:45.180 --> 00:24:49.840
Just how different the names are though, has
Croatia and Italy at loggerheads.

00:24:49.840 --> 00:24:53.169
Croatia has sought to trademark the name of
their Prošek with the European Commission

00:24:53.169 --> 00:24:57.539
under the assumption that consumers would
be able to differentiate it from Italian Prosecco.

00:24:57.539 --> 00:25:01.510
Italian wine aficionados think differently
and are fighting the move on account of potential

00:25:01.510 --> 00:25:02.510
confusion.

00:25:02.510 --> 00:25:06.720
Italians also see the effort as an attack
on Italian products more broadly, as Prosecco

00:25:06.720 --> 00:25:13.100
is a denomination of controlled origin–a
wine that only comes from a specific region.

00:25:13.100 --> 00:25:18.220
The world’s largest mammal, the blue whale,
only feeds in a few specific regions—one

00:25:18.220 --> 00:25:20.850
of which is off the coast of Chilean Patagonia.

00:25:20.850 --> 00:25:24.890
Unfortunately for the endangered species,
the water is also teeming with fishing vessels

00:25:24.890 --> 00:25:28.980
working the busy salmon farming industry,
with up to 1,000 boats a day passing through

00:25:28.980 --> 00:25:30.320
the feeding grounds.

00:25:30.320 --> 00:25:34.390
This traffic has led to a handful of fatal
collisions between boat and blue whale.

00:25:34.390 --> 00:25:38.350
With the regional population estimated to
be only in the hundreds, conservationists

00:25:38.350 --> 00:25:42.900
are scrambling to figure out a compromise
that gives the whales a bit more room.

00:25:42.900 --> 00:25:45.260
Bahrain is keen on finding a bit more room,
too.

00:25:45.260 --> 00:25:50.330
So keen, in fact, that the archipelago nation
announced plans to expand its landmass by

00:25:50.330 --> 00:25:51.330
60%.

00:25:51.330 --> 00:25:55.080
The island-building initiative will enlarge
Bahrain’s footprint, construct five new

00:25:55.080 --> 00:25:59.280
cities, and, the government hopes, attract
billions in foreign investment.

00:25:59.280 --> 00:26:04.350
The project is set to build out tourist attractions,
a “sport city,” and a commercial zone.

00:26:04.350 --> 00:26:09.570
From sport cities to sports washing, it was
a big year for professional athletics in Saudi

00:26:09.570 --> 00:26:10.570
Arabia.

00:26:10.570 --> 00:26:14.600
After its high-profile, highly controversial
takeover of Newcastle United, the country

00:26:14.600 --> 00:26:18.520
also announced a partnership between Golf
Saudi and the Asian Tour that’ll keep a

00:26:18.520 --> 00:26:22.740
Saudi stop on Asia’s preeminent golf circuit
and provide prize funding for a decade to

00:26:22.740 --> 00:26:23.740
come.

00:26:23.740 --> 00:26:27.529
While a quieter development than the Newcastle
deal, many denounced the move as another attempt

00:26:27.529 --> 00:26:31.809
to move conversation and attention away from
the country’s human rights record with glitz

00:26:31.809 --> 00:26:33.289
and games.

00:26:33.289 --> 00:26:37.679
Issues with human rights records will be impossible
to miss if the Chinese Fudan University is

00:26:37.679 --> 00:26:40.270
to follow through with building a campus in
Budapest, Hungary.

00:26:40.270 --> 00:26:44.260
A majority of the city’s population oppose
the project and the city’s mayor has called

00:26:44.260 --> 00:26:47.190
it an instance of “Chinese influence-buying.”

00:26:47.190 --> 00:26:51.160
Residents are becoming increasingly creative
in their pushback, recently renaming nearby

00:26:51.160 --> 00:26:55.360
streets Uyghur Martyrs’, Dalai Lama, and
Free Hong Kong Road.

00:26:55.360 --> 00:27:00.080
One car skipped the streets entirely on its
way from the Nitra airport in Slovakia to

00:27:00.080 --> 00:27:01.380
that in Bratislava.

00:27:01.380 --> 00:27:04.600
Instead, the prototype flew the 35-minute
route.

00:27:04.600 --> 00:27:09.289
For Klein Vision’s “Aircar,” it was
the 142nd landing, but an important first,

00:27:09.289 --> 00:27:13.029
too, as the car successfully transitioned
into normal car mode in just minutes.

00:27:13.029 --> 00:27:17.539
While behind on the timeline that science-fiction
authors envisioned, flying cars are slowly

00:27:17.539 --> 00:27:21.330
coming around with Klein, Hyundai, and GM
leading the way.

00:27:21.330 --> 00:27:25.070
Portugal’s parliament pushed into the future
of labor when it passed progressive measures

00:27:25.070 --> 00:27:27.590
to protect its increasingly online workforce.

00:27:27.590 --> 00:27:31.980
In response to the shift to working from home,
new laws bar employers from contacting employees

00:27:31.980 --> 00:27:35.860
during off-hours, allow parents of children
under eight to work from home without bosses’

00:27:35.860 --> 00:27:39.830
approval, and require employers to pitch in
on employees’ electricity costs.

00:27:39.830 --> 00:27:43.289
The move comes in response to the pandemic,
but also as an effort to protect Portugal’s

00:27:43.289 --> 00:27:47.690
reputation as an attractive place for digital
nomads to set up shop.

00:27:47.690 --> 00:27:51.640
A finding in the remains of a different sort
of nomad in Latvia cast doubt on previous

00:27:51.640 --> 00:27:56.420
theories as to the dramatic decline of stone-age
peoples across western Europe 5,000 years

00:27:56.420 --> 00:27:57.420
ago.

00:27:57.420 --> 00:28:01.460
DNA analysis of a hunter-gatherer showed the
man died of the plague, making him the earliest

00:28:01.460 --> 00:28:04.779
victim of what was thought to have caused
the mysterious population decline.

00:28:04.779 --> 00:28:08.919
Analysis, however, also showed that the strain
he carried didn’t spread easily and caused

00:28:08.919 --> 00:28:11.299
milder symptoms than iterations that would
follow.

00:28:11.299 --> 00:28:16.409
Now, rather than plague, scientists are looking
at climate change as a catalyst.

00:28:16.409 --> 00:28:19.720
Successful Spanish YouTubers are making like
wealthy bankers and professional athletes

00:28:19.720 --> 00:28:22.679
before them and running to the hills of Andorra.

00:28:22.679 --> 00:28:26.970
One Spanish creator called Andorra the “Silicon
Valley of YouTube,” as the country has quickly

00:28:26.970 --> 00:28:31.659
developed into a creative meeting place luring
in the like-minded with light taxes, relative

00:28:31.659 --> 00:28:34.159
anonymity, and less stringent lockdown policies.

00:28:34.159 --> 00:28:38.400
The move has been a boon for Andorra’s sputtering
economy, and a real loss for Spain’s, where

00:28:38.400 --> 00:28:43.529
local media has gone so far as to call Spanish
YouTubers relocating unpatriotic.

00:28:43.529 --> 00:28:48.710
A sputtering economy, many feel, would be
the result should Poland pivot away from coal.

00:28:48.710 --> 00:28:52.790
Currently 70% of the country’s energy comes
from the non-renewable super-polluter, and

00:28:52.790 --> 00:28:56.030
coal companies and miner unions hold serious
political power.

00:28:56.030 --> 00:28:59.830
But Poland’s appetite and the massive strip
mine on its border are running Czech wells

00:28:59.830 --> 00:29:03.020
dry, or at least so the Czech Republic accuses.

00:29:03.020 --> 00:29:07.350
Citing European environmental laws, the Czech
Republic has sued Poland, setting off a wave

00:29:07.350 --> 00:29:10.520
of conspiracy theories across coal country.

00:29:10.520 --> 00:29:13.929
Conspiratorial might seem like a good way
to describe Lithuania’s defense ministry

00:29:13.929 --> 00:29:17.770
calling for citizens to throw their Chinese-made
cell phones away.

00:29:17.770 --> 00:29:21.890
The request, though, comes after the nation’s
cyber security center found that the Xiomi

00:29:21.890 --> 00:29:27.679
Corp, a Chinese phone-maker, have censor technology
built into devices that track 449 terms including

00:29:27.679 --> 00:29:30.830
the likes of “free Tibet,” and “democracy
movement.”

00:29:30.830 --> 00:29:35.840
The finding comes as relationships between
China and Lithuania sour over Taiwan.

00:29:35.840 --> 00:29:40.860
One internationally recognized state, one
defiant self-identifying state, two UK military

00:29:40.860 --> 00:29:46.230
bases, and one UN buffer zone to keep the
peace hint at Cyprus' geopolitical complexity.

00:29:46.230 --> 00:29:50.290
Things didn’t get any simpler in 2021 when
Turkish President Erdoğan announced that

00:29:50.290 --> 00:29:54.350
in celebration of the 47th anniversary of
Turkey invading the island, the country planned

00:29:54.350 --> 00:29:58.210
to resettle an abandoned, and formerly Greek
Cypriot tourist town.

00:29:58.210 --> 00:30:02.080
Celebrating an invasion with a different sort
of invasion has received poor marks from the

00:30:02.080 --> 00:30:04.200
US, the UN, and Greek Cypriots.

00:30:04.200 --> 00:30:09.850
While heated geopolitical relations, and politicians’
hot air pose a threat in the Mediterranean,

00:30:09.850 --> 00:30:11.960
so too does literal heat.

00:30:11.960 --> 00:30:15.820
Greece, particularly vulnerable to climate
change generally, and especially heatwaves,

00:30:15.820 --> 00:30:19.299
has decided to begin to name the extreme bouts
of heat.

00:30:19.299 --> 00:30:23.279
Categorizing heatwaves is tricky, but any
standardization will allow the country to

00:30:23.279 --> 00:30:27.710
better systematically respond to temperature
upticks and communicate the danger.

00:30:27.710 --> 00:30:32.679
2021 marked the end of the Free Latifa campaign,
as the movement hatched three years ago finally

00:30:32.679 --> 00:30:34.480
saw its vision come to fruition.

00:30:34.480 --> 00:30:38.830
Princess Latifa was captured by her father,
Dubai’s Sheikh Mohammed bin Rashid al-Maktoum,

00:30:38.830 --> 00:30:43.270
when trying to express a little self-determination
and leave the United Arab Emirates.

00:30:43.270 --> 00:30:46.779
She had hardly been seen in the past three
years but it seems her confinement came to

00:30:46.779 --> 00:30:51.159
an abrupt end as an Instagram photo showed
the princess traveling in Iceland and a verifiable

00:30:51.159 --> 00:30:55.279
statement quoted her saying she could now
“travel where I want.”

00:30:55.279 --> 00:30:59.470
Italian motorcyclists and golfers can now,
within reason, travel where they want, too,

00:30:59.470 --> 00:31:00.770
and do so in style.

00:31:00.770 --> 00:31:04.790
The historic Italian car company, Iso, is
relaunching with a young backer from a famed

00:31:04.790 --> 00:31:06.149
lineage leading the way.

00:31:06.149 --> 00:31:09.940
Catching the company up with the present and
charging it into the future, Ferruccio Lamborghini

00:31:09.940 --> 00:31:15.120
and team are launching a motorcycle and golf
cart that are modern, stylish, and sustainable—both

00:31:15.120 --> 00:31:17.159
vehicles are completely electric.

00:31:17.159 --> 00:31:21.769
A scarecrow of the seas may help to save the
lives of thousands of seabirds each year thanks

00:31:21.769 --> 00:31:25.539
to researchers in Estonia who helped develop
a buoy with googly eyes.

00:31:25.539 --> 00:31:29.790
The device floats above small-scale fishing
operation gill nets, which can be lethal to

00:31:29.790 --> 00:31:32.510
diving seabirds, and deters them from coming
near.

00:31:32.510 --> 00:31:36.840
In fact, scientists found it reduced the congregating
birds by about a quarter who are turned off

00:31:36.840 --> 00:31:40.200
by eye contact and erratic buoy behavior.

00:31:40.200 --> 00:31:43.919
Another sort of deterrent is the addition
of Malta to an international greylist kept

00:31:43.919 --> 00:31:48.510
by Financial Action Task Force, a watchdog
organization meant to monitor money laundering

00:31:48.510 --> 00:31:49.799
and terrorism funding.

00:31:49.799 --> 00:31:53.730
In recent years, the island nation’s low
tax rate for foreign companies has attracted

00:31:53.730 --> 00:31:57.370
substantial banking and investment, but that
also makes it ripe for abuse.

00:31:57.370 --> 00:32:00.850
It’s the first European Union nation to
be listed, and could potentially affect the

00:32:00.850 --> 00:32:05.919
upward trajectory of Malta as wealthy investors
look to alternate locations given its now-tenuous

00:32:05.919 --> 00:32:06.919
nature.

00:32:06.919 --> 00:32:10.730
One of Europe’s wealthiest people and the
Czech Republic’s richest man, Peter Kellner,

00:32:10.730 --> 00:32:15.140
was tragically killed in a helicopter crash
while heli-skiing in Alaska, along with four

00:32:15.140 --> 00:32:16.480
additional passengers.

00:32:16.480 --> 00:32:22.280
Kellner was estimated to be worth $17.5 billion,
and his death follows a string of recent fatal

00:32:22.280 --> 00:32:26.790
high-profile helicopter accidents including
Kobe Bryant and French billionaire Olivier

00:32:26.790 --> 00:32:27.790
Dassault.

00:32:27.790 --> 00:32:31.960
On the coast, France and the United Kingdom
finally settled some post-Brexit bickering

00:32:31.960 --> 00:32:32.960
over fishing.

00:32:32.960 --> 00:32:36.300
France wanted the British government to issue
a number of fishing licenses to small French

00:32:36.300 --> 00:32:40.060
boats so they could continue harvesting in
British waters, and the Brits stalled, citing

00:32:40.060 --> 00:32:42.330
a number of technicalities from the French
side.

00:32:42.330 --> 00:32:46.360
The issue simmered to a threat-of-trade-sanctions
level, but cooler heads prevailed, an agreement

00:32:46.360 --> 00:32:51.450
was met, and 83 fishing licenses were assigned
before it reached a boiling point.

00:32:51.450 --> 00:32:55.029
Another agreement was reached in Spain, but
this one pertains to many people’s go-to

00:32:55.029 --> 00:32:58.000
source for the day’s headlines: Google news.

00:32:58.000 --> 00:33:01.510
Banned from the country for six years because
Spain required Google to pay a central fee

00:33:01.510 --> 00:33:06.340
to media organizations for use of their stories,
the new law now allows Google parent company,

00:33:06.340 --> 00:33:09.210
Alphabet, to negotiate directly with publishers
for content.

00:33:09.210 --> 00:33:15.110
Now, more than 1,000 Spanish media organizations
can be sourced for news from a single smartphone.

00:33:15.110 --> 00:33:18.760
Speaking of smartphones, it may have gone
unnoticed in your Apple-happy world, but South

00:33:18.760 --> 00:33:23.070
Korean manufacturer LG announced its departure
from the phone market.

00:33:23.070 --> 00:33:26.500
Once ranked only behind Apple and Samsung
for smartphone manufacturing, the company

00:33:26.500 --> 00:33:30.799
said a series of bad reviews and technical
rollouts prompted it to shift its focus to

00:33:30.799 --> 00:33:35.440
other areas, such as connected devices for
the home, robotics, and artificial intelligence.

00:33:35.440 --> 00:33:39.720
LG joins Ericsson and HTC in the cell phone
graveyard.

00:33:39.720 --> 00:33:42.230
Smart is also the way to describe Amazon’s
accountants.

00:33:42.230 --> 00:33:47.441
The company had a record-breaking 2020 in
Europe, hauling in some $50 billion, but it

00:33:47.441 --> 00:33:51.970
managed to pay zero in corporate taxes to
Luxembourg, home to its European headquarters.

00:33:51.970 --> 00:33:55.659
Of course, it’s all legal, but when a company
not only doesn’t pay anything, but also

00:33:55.659 --> 00:34:00.390
declares losses which result in tax credits,
to the tune of $63 million, there is some

00:34:00.390 --> 00:34:04.900
definite eye-rolling and belt-tightening from
policymakers looking to benefit from the boom.

00:34:04.900 --> 00:34:09.100
The government in Slovenia is running an alleged
crusade against culture, with Prime Minister

00:34:09.100 --> 00:34:13.180
Janez Jansa replacing the heads of several
arts organizations in what some are calling

00:34:13.180 --> 00:34:15.230
a shift to more conservative approaches.

00:34:15.230 --> 00:34:19.300
Jansa, who had served twice in the role prior
to being ousted for corruption, named new

00:34:19.300 --> 00:34:23.770
leaders for the National Museum, the Museum
of Contemporary History, and the Moderna Galerija,

00:34:23.770 --> 00:34:27.460
and he continues to terminate leases from
arts organizations that rent space from the

00:34:27.460 --> 00:34:28.460
government.

00:34:28.460 --> 00:34:32.389
He denies that it’s an orchestrated movement,
but for many, it’s hard to paint over the

00:34:32.389 --> 00:34:33.389
facts.

00:34:33.389 --> 00:34:37.820
Low government limitations have led to a hot
streak of gambling development in Lichtenstein,

00:34:37.820 --> 00:34:40.919
one of the world’s smallest countries, now
home to five casinos.

00:34:40.919 --> 00:34:45.660
That may sound like a so-so number, but it
puts its per capita above Monaco, Macau, and

00:34:45.660 --> 00:34:47.329
Las Vegas’ Clark County.

00:34:47.329 --> 00:34:48.329
One reason?

00:34:48.329 --> 00:34:51.990
The gambling tax rate is lower than in neighboring
countries, and the government there hasn’t

00:34:51.990 --> 00:34:54.580
set caps on the number of casinos that can
be built.

00:34:54.580 --> 00:34:58.089
Five more are in the pipeline, which means
the foreign investors largely responsible

00:34:58.089 --> 00:35:01.030
for them are betting big on the future.

00:35:01.030 --> 00:35:04.220
Tensions are rising between Japan and the
tandem of China and Russia.

00:35:04.220 --> 00:35:07.510
While they’ve been escalating for years
because of Beijing’s increased presence

00:35:07.510 --> 00:35:12.510
on islands controlled by Japan but claimed
by Russia, they hit a new high when a 10-ship

00:35:12.510 --> 00:35:16.190
Chinese-Russian flotilla circumnavigated Japan’s
main island this summer.

00:35:16.190 --> 00:35:20.210
China and Russia say it was merely a diplomatic
exercise, but Japan is worried a threatening

00:35:20.210 --> 00:35:25.040
presence means it will need to increase defense
spending and be more on guard.

00:35:25.040 --> 00:35:28.810
Spying seems to be a trend, but the United
States told Israel they don’t want to play

00:35:28.810 --> 00:35:29.970
that game.

00:35:29.970 --> 00:35:34.200
Israeli spyware maker NSO Group was placed
on an American blacklist after it was reasonably

00:35:34.200 --> 00:35:39.030
confirmed that NSO’s signature product,
Pegasus, was used by foreign governments against

00:35:39.030 --> 00:35:41.599
dissidents, journalists, diplomats, and clergy
members.

00:35:41.599 --> 00:35:45.560
The blacklisting means, among other things,
that NSO won’t be able to buy components

00:35:45.560 --> 00:35:49.490
from US companies for its products—something
Apple is ensuring after suing the group this

00:35:49.490 --> 00:35:51.030
year as well.

00:35:51.030 --> 00:35:54.690
Austrian tourism officials want to encourage
viewing of the country’s nude sculptures

00:35:54.690 --> 00:35:58.560
and paintings that pepper museums, but social
media platforms’ censorship policies have

00:35:58.560 --> 00:36:00.470
made their promotion difficult.

00:36:00.470 --> 00:36:04.401
So Vienna did what anyone trying to get around
the no-private-parts policy would do: they

00:36:04.401 --> 00:36:08.000
opened an account on the adults-only app OnlyFans.

00:36:08.000 --> 00:36:11.250
Many of the works are critical to national
cultural history, and now they’re free to

00:36:11.250 --> 00:36:14.360
promote the exhibitions without that fuzzy
bar.

00:36:14.360 --> 00:36:19.740
2021 wasn’t all spying, censorship, and
general contention, there were positive developments

00:36:19.740 --> 00:36:24.820
too: United States-based dictionary.com named
“allyship” its word of the year.

00:36:24.820 --> 00:36:28.890
Officially added to dictionary.com in 2021,
“allyship” rose in popularity during the

00:36:28.890 --> 00:36:32.730
Black Lives Matter movements across the world
but its definition makes clear that its applications

00:36:32.730 --> 00:36:34.020
are even farther-reaching.

00:36:34.020 --> 00:36:39.310
One says, "the role of a person who advocates
for inclusion of a marginalized or politicized

00:36:39.310 --> 00:36:41.829
group in solidarity but not as a member.”

00:36:41.829 --> 00:36:45.630
More word searches means there’s certainly
more of this going on.

00:36:45.630 --> 00:36:49.360
This is a story about the good guy winning,
but this time, it’s a lobster.

00:36:49.360 --> 00:36:53.440
A Canadian grocer noticed that no one was
purchasing a certain carrot-colored crustacean,

00:36:53.440 --> 00:36:57.750
and on top of that, it was being picked on
by other lobsters in the tank.

00:36:57.750 --> 00:37:01.350
After several weeks he bought the lobster
himself and donated it to the Toronto Aquarium,

00:37:01.350 --> 00:37:05.350
where it was discovered his strange hue was
a one-in-30 million genetic mutation.

00:37:05.350 --> 00:37:10.760
Pinchy, the lobster, avoided the plate and
now has a more permanent, public home.

00:37:10.760 --> 00:37:14.470
In an effort to speed up the development of
more home building in New Zealand, to combat

00:37:14.470 --> 00:37:18.900
the 30% increase in housing cost and shortage
of inventory, officials are cutting red tape

00:37:18.900 --> 00:37:22.630
and making it easier for developers to address
a housing crisis so dire that it’s drawn

00:37:22.630 --> 00:37:24.680
international attention.

00:37:24.680 --> 00:37:27.990
Specifically they’re changing some density
regulations, allowing for up to three homes

00:37:27.990 --> 00:37:32.420
of three stories on one site versus one home
of two stories, a move that some predict will

00:37:32.420 --> 00:37:37.770
erect 48,000 to 106,000 new homes in the next
five to eight years.

00:37:37.770 --> 00:37:41.470
Expansion is something that a Belgian farmer
accidentally did when he moved a several-hundred

00:37:41.470 --> 00:37:43.859
pound stone seven feet into France.

00:37:43.859 --> 00:37:47.450
The historic markers delineate the borders
between the two countries, and a team of Frenchmen

00:37:47.450 --> 00:37:51.810
who patrol the remote countryside verifying
the positions noticed the errant stone.

00:37:51.810 --> 00:37:56.060
Luckily, the farmer wasn’t charged with
violating the international treaty that certifies

00:37:56.060 --> 00:38:00.160
the border—a crime that could have resulted
in a territorial war instead of a slap on

00:38:00.160 --> 00:38:01.170
the wrist.

00:38:01.170 --> 00:38:05.560
To the north, the United Kingdom is rapidly
trying to make up for centuries of contributing

00:38:05.560 --> 00:38:06.680
to climate change.

00:38:06.680 --> 00:38:10.770
To that end, it launched the world’s most
powerful tidal turbine off the Port of Dundee,

00:38:10.770 --> 00:38:14.650
creating enough electricity for 2,000 homes,
and Rolls Royce announced the development

00:38:14.650 --> 00:38:19.220
of 16 smaller, cheaper nuclear power plants
to electrify 1 million homes.

00:38:19.220 --> 00:38:24.010
Britain is already one of the largest wind-energy
producers in the world–not bad for the country

00:38:24.010 --> 00:38:25.780
that started the Industrial Revolution.

00:38:25.780 --> 00:38:29.020
Have you heard of Grab or a SPAC?

00:38:29.020 --> 00:38:31.060
In this story, we have both.

00:38:31.060 --> 00:38:35.800
Grab is a Singapore-based superapp that offers
everything from ride sharing to banking in

00:38:35.800 --> 00:38:37.160
one tap.

00:38:37.160 --> 00:38:41.390
SPAC is a special purpose acquisition company,
an investment strategy in which a larger company

00:38:41.390 --> 00:38:45.500
merges with a publicly-traded shell company
in order to expedite going public.

00:38:45.500 --> 00:38:50.221
Grab signed a $39.5 billion merger deal with
a US SPAC, which brought the company public

00:38:50.221 --> 00:38:52.869
on the NASDAQ stock exchange on December 2nd.

00:38:52.869 --> 00:38:56.310
That makes it the largest-ever deal of its
kind, and means we should pay attention to

00:38:56.310 --> 00:38:59.099
both SPACs and Grab ASAP.

00:38:59.099 --> 00:39:03.280
Finland has a lot going for it, including
being named the happiest country in the world

00:39:03.280 --> 00:39:04.950
for the fourth consecutive year.

00:39:04.950 --> 00:39:10.170
But, one thing it can’t nail is labor retention,
and, in fact one study shows a major reason

00:39:10.170 --> 00:39:14.740
foreign students leave Helsinki within their
first year of graduating is the language barrier.

00:39:14.740 --> 00:39:18.070
These difficulties prompted the mayor to suggest
transitioning the capital city to speaking

00:39:18.070 --> 00:39:19.140
English primarily.

00:39:19.140 --> 00:39:22.339
That may help employment, but TBD on happiness.

00:39:22.339 --> 00:39:26.260
We’ve talked a lot about ways to create
green energy.

00:39:26.260 --> 00:39:29.660
Another way to fight climate change is by
consuming less meat, and Denmark is leading

00:39:29.660 --> 00:39:34.550
the European Union in this effort by giving
$90 million to farmers who produce plant-based

00:39:34.550 --> 00:39:36.320
foods over the next five years.

00:39:36.320 --> 00:39:40.160
The country eats a lot of pork, but the sale
of plant-based food there has increased by

00:39:40.160 --> 00:39:42.560
$8 million in two years.

00:39:42.560 --> 00:39:47.000
Pigs might not fly, and they might not be
the only thing on the menu anymore either.

00:39:47.000 --> 00:39:50.830
Just to the southwest, officials in the Netherlands
unveiled a plan to reduce the country’s

00:39:50.830 --> 00:39:53.210
livestock by about 1/3 over the next 13 years.

00:39:53.210 --> 00:39:57.060
But it’s for a different reason: there’s
too much poop.

00:39:57.060 --> 00:40:01.440
The country has more than 100 million cattle,
chickens, and pigs—the highest density in

00:40:01.440 --> 00:40:05.150
Europe—and can’t quite contain their waste
without polluting important waterways.

00:40:05.150 --> 00:40:09.090
Farmers, naturally, are pushing back, even
though the multi-billion dollar plan intends

00:40:09.090 --> 00:40:11.480
to pay them to essentially exit the industry.

00:40:11.480 --> 00:40:14.730
Maybe they can jump on Denmark’s plant-based
patty-wagon.

00:40:14.730 --> 00:40:18.500
Also planning for the future is the 2032 Olympic
committee, and specifically, Australia.

00:40:18.500 --> 00:40:21.869
It was announced that Brisbane will be the
host of the summer games in 10 years, and

00:40:21.869 --> 00:40:25.490
what’s notable about this selection isn’t
the place, but the process.

00:40:25.490 --> 00:40:29.700
Instead of expensive, competitive, and often
corrupt bidding wars pitting cities against

00:40:29.700 --> 00:40:33.790
one another, bids are now submitted and then
reviewed behind closed doors by selection

00:40:33.790 --> 00:40:34.790
committees.

00:40:34.790 --> 00:40:38.140
In this case, the best mate won.

00:40:38.140 --> 00:40:41.830
In Sweden, Magdalena Andersson won but wasn’t
too happy with her first day on the job.

00:40:41.830 --> 00:40:45.780
So, the Swedish prime minister resigned just
12 hours in because the junior Green party

00:40:45.780 --> 00:40:49.500
also quit, throwing her coalition into chaos.

00:40:49.500 --> 00:40:53.010
She indicated she’d lead a Social Democrat
single-party and was reelected a week later,

00:40:53.010 --> 00:40:56.630
becoming the first female prime minister of
Sweden—for a second time.

00:40:56.630 --> 00:41:00.880
The second time was not as successful for
a criminal in Germany, whose first crime involved

00:41:00.880 --> 00:41:02.590
a burglary in 2012.

00:41:02.590 --> 00:41:06.810
He got away with that one and a bite of a
sausage, which left behind some DNA evidence

00:41:06.810 --> 00:41:08.250
that police held onto.

00:41:08.250 --> 00:41:11.610
Fast forward to today when he committed a
more violent crime and the genetic residue

00:41:11.610 --> 00:41:15.470
linked him to the decade-old heist through
an international information-sharing library.

00:41:15.470 --> 00:41:19.801
However, the statute of limitations expired
and he’s gone free, proving there’s no

00:41:19.801 --> 00:41:22.150
bite out of crime this time.

00:41:22.150 --> 00:41:25.630
So we’re five from the end, and the truth
is, a lot of headlines you missed are about

00:41:25.630 --> 00:41:30.060
the ways these recent, more developed countries
are adapting and attacking climate change.

00:41:30.060 --> 00:41:34.440
Iceland started operating the world’s first
direct air capture technology, which turns

00:41:34.440 --> 00:41:35.640
CO2 into rock.

00:41:35.640 --> 00:41:39.060
But perhaps more quirky is that the country
also performed the world’s first double

00:41:39.060 --> 00:41:42.849
arm-and-shoulder transplant to replace the
limbs a man lost in a work accident more than

00:41:42.849 --> 00:41:44.550
two decades prior.

00:41:44.550 --> 00:41:48.660
Progress on the micro and the macro level
is something to high-five about.

00:41:48.660 --> 00:41:55.849
Now a quick disclaimer before this next story:
the UN lists 189 HDI scores, and while a vast

00:41:55.849 --> 00:41:59.460
majority of those scores correlate to countries,
the UN makes sure to acknowledge their list

00:41:59.460 --> 00:42:03.490
is a compilation of “189 countries and UN-recognized
territories.”

00:42:03.490 --> 00:42:07.880
We have now arrived at the only territory
on their list, and while technically not a

00:42:07.880 --> 00:42:11.420
country, we figured the more news the better,
so we’ve gone ahead and included the Chinese

00:42:11.420 --> 00:42:13.319
territory of Hong Kong.

00:42:13.319 --> 00:42:18.070
Disney+ finally launched in Hong Kong in 2021
and while much of the streaming service’s

00:42:18.070 --> 00:42:21.030
content provides a needed escape from the
chaos and confusion that’s embroiled the

00:42:21.030 --> 00:42:24.600
Chinese territory in the past few years, one
omission from the Simpson’s catalog hints

00:42:24.600 --> 00:42:27.590
at just how inescapable the tension has become.

00:42:27.590 --> 00:42:32.369
Noticeably absent was episode 12 of season
16 that has the Simpson family visiting China

00:42:32.369 --> 00:42:36.220
and specifically Tiananmen square, and while
minor for plot purposes, its disappearance

00:42:36.220 --> 00:42:39.880
signals the increasing reach of government
censorship into the traditionally independent

00:42:39.880 --> 00:42:40.880
city.

00:42:40.880 --> 00:42:45.840
The Swiss are notoriously on time, but they
were late to join the same-sex marriage party.

00:42:45.840 --> 00:42:49.640
The country finally approved a “Marriage
for All” initiative with two-thirds voting

00:42:49.640 --> 00:42:53.700
in favor, becoming one of the last Western
European countries to do so.

00:42:53.700 --> 00:42:57.859
Switzerland, known for neutrality, is slow
on inclusivity issues and didn’t allow women

00:42:57.859 --> 00:42:59.700
the right to vote until 1971.

00:42:59.700 --> 00:43:03.720
So this, though sluggish in adoption, is a
cultural win.

00:43:03.720 --> 00:43:07.800
It also took a while for Irish authorities
to come down on enforcing the European Union’s

00:43:07.800 --> 00:43:12.240
three-year-old General Data Protection Regulation,
which is a comprehensive data privacy law.

00:43:12.240 --> 00:43:17.660
But, they served Meta’s Whatsapp with a
$270 million fine for not being transparent

00:43:17.660 --> 00:43:21.060
on how it uses people’s data across the
company’s platforms.

00:43:21.060 --> 00:43:24.829
Many tech company’s headquarters are based
in Ireland, where corporate tax rates are

00:43:24.829 --> 00:43:28.480
low, so there may be more cases like this—which
of course is being contested by Whatsapp—to

00:43:28.480 --> 00:43:29.480
come.

00:43:29.480 --> 00:43:34.420
And finally, it feels appropriate to end on
a note that reminds us about the scale of

00:43:34.420 --> 00:43:35.420
humanity.

00:43:35.420 --> 00:43:39.570
In Norway, a large meteor lit up the summer
night sky for five to six seconds before,

00:43:39.570 --> 00:43:44.170
in all likelihood, crashing into a densely
wooded area about 40 miles, or 60 kilometers,

00:43:44.170 --> 00:43:45.720
west of the country’s capital.

00:43:45.720 --> 00:43:49.310
Some people reported a strong wind created
by the pressure from it, and while it may

00:43:49.310 --> 00:43:53.670
take years to find its physical remains, the
blazing meteor, for a fleeting moment, captured

00:43:53.670 --> 00:43:59.340
the attention of thousands of onlookers–a
rare instance of singularity in an ever-individual

00:43:59.340 --> 00:44:00.340
world.

00:44:00.340 --> 00:44:04.930
Of course, the news doesn’t stop with Norway,
nor does it end with the end of the year.

